#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065097} :activity/id #uuid "0292b7a3-d5c9-54a7-ba7c-938624bcc457" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049847 :topic/id #uuid "18636612-788d-519b-97ca-16774367f5ac" :topic/math-academy-id 360} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065097 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065441 :tutorial/content "When we want to calculate the **square of a binomial**, like\n\n$$\n(a+b)^2\n$$\n\nthere's a formula that we can use instead of working out the product $(a+b)(a+b)$ manually. The formula is\n\n$$\n(a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2\n$$\n\nIt might be helpful to remember this as *\"the square of the first term, plus the square of the second term, plus twice the product.\"*\n\nSuppose we need to calculate the square $(x+3)^2$. In this case, we have $a= x$ and $b=3$. We substitute into the formula and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x + 3)^{2} &=  \\\\\n(x)^{2} + 2(x)(3) + (3)^{2} &=  \\\\\n&= x^{2} + 6x + 9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can check that the formula gives the correct result by working out the multiplication manually:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} (x + 3)^2 \\\\[3pt] &= (x + 3)(x + 3) \\\\[3pt] &= x(x + 3) + 3(x + 3) \\\\[3pt] &= x^2 + 3x + 3x + 9 \\\\[3pt] &= x^2 + 6x + 9 &\\, {\\color{green}{\\checkmark}} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the same result! But by using the formula, we save a lot of time and effort." :tutorial/id #uuid "0266d886-b5db-53fe-bc51-f6486beb6eef" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8878 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "ee3a0134-3957-5b1c-b05a-a30af1c8709d" :step/math-academy-id 170779 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065098}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065098 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064232 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063991 :question/id #uuid "70f19ea4-d0b8-537a-8ae4-06a236cf37cf" :question/math-academy-id "e-14318"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "288c08af-0583-5588-b767-4254544cf70c" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050818}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064590} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064678} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064749}] :knowledge-point/title "Squaring Linear Binomials"} :step/id #uuid "39924b31-d2c9-5359-be1b-3c04f7ad4699" :step/math-academy-id 170780 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065099}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065099 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064233 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063992 :question/id #uuid "c1a6df9e-b1e8-51c8-b5df-4cc624e14193" :question/math-academy-id "e-14319"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "63291c46-6a0f-5e7c-ab0a-acba80fe58f3" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064592} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064593} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064729}] :knowledge-point/title "Squaring Nonlinear Binomials"} :step/id #uuid "9b092f72-50ae-5b82-96c3-f01cc623e041" :step/math-academy-id 170784 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065100}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065100 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065442 :tutorial/content "So far, we've been using the formula for the square of a binomial involving addition:\n\n$$\n(a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2\n$$\n\nThere is also a similar formula that we can use to compute the square of a binomial involving subtraction. The formula is\n\n$$\n(a - b)^2 = a^2 - 2ab + b^2\n$$\n\nFor example, to compute the square $(x-3)^2$, we can substitute $a=x$ and $b=3$ into the formula and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - 3)^{2} &=  \\\\\n(x)^{2} - 2(x)(3) + (3)^{2} &=  \\\\\n&= x^{2} - 6x + 9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can check that the formula gives the correct result by working out the multiplication manually:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} (x - 3)^2 \\\\ &= (x - 3)(x - 3) \\\\ &= x(x - 3) - 3(x - 3) \\\\ &= x^2 - 3x - 3x + 9 \\\\ &= x^2 - 6x + 9 &\\, {\\color{green}{\\checkmark}} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we get the same result." :tutorial/id #uuid "e42b96f5-ca3b-588b-8931-106b975bd0ac" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8879 :tutorial/title "Binomials With Subtraction"} :step/id #uuid "13d60779-951a-5265-8019-e1ca3444406c" :step/math-academy-id 170788 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065101}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065101 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064234 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063993 :question/id #uuid "487f1c4c-63c9-51cf-9a0e-7d9bc0a4c7c7" :question/math-academy-id "e-14320"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "afd30bc7-dce9-5e03-a213-2b9695e39091" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064591} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064594} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064679}] :knowledge-point/title "Squaring Binomials With Subtraction"} :step/id #uuid "2fb2e377-ee0a-5a7e-a9fc-c5e5d9b5786a" :step/math-academy-id 170789}] :activity/title "Squaring Binomials" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186064447}]}
